From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msspellcheckingfacility: the Spell Checking API over hunspell (7010)

Programs that check spelling through ISpellCheckerFactory (CLSID_SpellCheckerFactory)
found no class: HexChat's spell checker (enchant's "win8" provider) failed with
"init_enchant_provider returned invalid provider". The new msspellcheckingfacility.dll
registers the factory over the system's hunspell dictionaries. libhunspell is
loaded at run time on the unix side; the dictionaries are found in /usr/share/hunspell,
so it needs no Z: drive. It provides:
- languages, with a bare language resolving to its installed variant;
- Check and ComprehensiveCheck (misspellings, repeated words; addresses, links and
  words with digits are skipped);
- Suggest, Ignore, Add and Remove (ISpellChecker2), AutoCorrect, the change event;
- the user's word lists in %APPDATA%\Microsoft\Spelling\<tag>
  (default.dic/.exc/.acl) and IUserDictionariesRegistrar.
include/spellcheck.idl is new.
